{"id":1847822,"retrievedAt":"2026-11-27T20:16:12.156Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":16,"name":"Animation"},{"id":27,"name":"Horror"},{"id":878,"name":"Science Fiction"}],"homepage":"https://slimeengine.com/fy202411","id":1847822,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["CN"],"original_language":"zh","original_title":"臭水沟的毒虫不断往我身上爬","overview":"The video work \"The Venomous Creatures From The Gutter Keep Crawing Onto Me\" employs a complex CG production process to capture fragments of childhood memory: the eerie magenta sky after a steel factory explosion, the recurring shadows of the rear-eight-wheel cement mixers managed by the artist’s father, and ghostly apparitions surfacing in the molten iron of the steel furnace. This piece unveils the gaps within cultural memory between the individual and the collective. Using horror-tinged CG imagery, Fang Yang draws visual elements from cartoons, cinema, and personal memories to evoke a nostalgic resonance with cult and tokusatsu films. The distortion in the visuals and the pulsating procedural textures serve not only as metaphors for real-world anxiety and unease but also as a profound examination of individual identity.","popularity":0.1164,"poster_path":"/2nnmITvlShNJIEUpbk0pt30Ypse.jpg","production_companies":[{"id":321468,"logo_path":null,"name":"Slime Engine","origin_country":""}],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"CN","name":"China"}],"release_date":"2024-10-29","revenue":0,"runtime":11,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[{"english_name":"Chinese","iso_639_1":"zh","name":"汉语"},{"english_name":"English","iso_639_1":"en","name":"English"}],"status":"Released","tagline":"It's not who I am underneath, but what I do that defines me","title":"The Venomous Creatures From The Gutter Keep Crawling Onto Me","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[],"crew":[{"adult":false,"gender":0,"id":6699732,"kn